Quick getting‑started (recommended: SvelteKit for full web apps)
- Prereqs: Node (16+; 18+ recommended), npm/pnpm/yarn.
- Create a new SvelteKit app:
  - npm create svelte@latest my-app
  - cd my-app
  - npm install
  - npm run dev
  - Open the dev server (usually http://localhost:5173).
  (If you only want a single‑page Svelte app instead of SvelteKit, use: npm init vite@latest my-app -- --template svelte)

Core Svelte concepts (fast overview)
- Components: .svelte files contain <script>, markup, and <style> in one file.
- Props: export let name;
- Reactivity:
  - Reactive assignments: $: doubled = count * 2
  - Reactive stores: import { writable } from 'svelte/store'; use $storeName in templates
- Event binding: <button on:click={handleClick}>Click</button>
- Two‑way binding: <input bind:value={value} />
- Conditionals & loops: {#if ...}{:else}{/if}, {#each items as item}{/each}
- Lifecycle: import { onMount, beforeUpdate, afterUpdate, onDestroy } from 'svelte'
- Transitions/animations: import { fade, fly } from 'svelte/transition' and use in:fade

Tiny example (Counter.svelte)
<script>
  export let initial = 0;
  let count = initial;
  function inc() { count += 1; }
  $: doubled = count * 2;
</script>

<button on:click={inc}>
  Count: {count} — double: {doubled}
</button>

Using stores
<script>
  import { writable } from 'svelte/store';
  export const user = writable(null);
</script>
In components read/write with $user.

SvelteKit: recommended for web apps
- File‑based routing: src/routes/+page.svelte for pages, dynamic routes with [id].
- Layouts: +layout.svelte for shared UI.
- Data loading: +page.server.js/ts or +page.js/ts with load() functions (server/client contexts).
- SSR, CSR, SSG/prerendering supported.
- Adapters for deployment: adapter-vercel, adapter-netlify, adapter-static, etc.
- Build: npm run build, then deploy using your chosen adapter/hosting.

Build & deploy
- Build: npm run build
- Use SvelteKit adapters or build static with adapter-static.
- Common hosts: Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare Pages, static CDNs.

Tooling & testing
- TypeScript support built in (choose at project init)
- Use Vitest for unit tests, Playwright or Cypress for e2e
- Linting/formatting: ESLint + Prettier or community configs

Libraries & ecosystem
- Component libraries: Svelte Material UI, Carbon for Svelte, Flowbite‑Svelte, etc.
- Router for SPA only apps: svelte-spa-router (but SvelteKit covers routing for most apps)
- UI & animation helpers in svelte/transition and svelte/motion

Tips & best practices
- Prefer SvelteKit for full apps (routing, SSR, endpoints).
- Keep component state local; use stores for cross‑component shared state.
- Use file‑based routing and +layout for consistent page chrome.
- Profile and trust Svelte’s compile‑time optimizations — fewer re-renders than VDOM frameworks.

Resources
- Official docs: svelte.dev (language) and kit.svelte.dev (SvelteKit)
- Svelte REPL for prototyping components quickly

